{#- Lore the KEYWORD rule missed, pulled back by embedding similarity
    (context/semantic.py). Kept apart from world_info.j2 for one reason, and
    it is a packing reason rather than a presentational one: the packer drops
    sections whole and picks the largest in a tier first, so folding these in
    would have grown the World info section and could have dropped every
    keyword hit with them -- the opposite of what a layer that only adds is
    supposed to do. Here they sit in the archive tier, first to go.
    Secret entries (#49) carry the same heading they get one section up —
    recall is a way of REACHING an entry, not a licence to publish it.
    Vars: recalled_lore_bodies ([str]), secret_recalled_lore_bodies ([str]). -#}
{%- from "scene/_secrecy.j2" import secret_block -%}
{%- set public = recalled_lore_bodies | select | list -%}
{%- set secret = secret_recalled_lore_bodies | select | list -%}
{{ [public | join("\n\n"), secret_block(secret) if secret else ""] | select | join("\n\n") }}
